        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "The netlist places U4 pin 27 (VCOMH) on the GND net, and both terminals of C11 are also on the GND net. The SPICE deck models C11 as a capacitor from ground to ground.",
      "expected": "C11 should connect U4 VCOMH to GND: one terminal on the VCOMH node and the other terminal on GND. VCOMH is the charge-pump output and should not be shorted to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"27\") (pinfunction \"VCOMH\") (pintype \"output\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C11 0 0 4.7u"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C11 (4.7 µF) — U4 `VCOMH` (charge-pump output) to GND, the output reservoir/filter cap"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The SSD1306 charge-pump output is shorted to ground and the reservoir capacitor is effectively bypassed/shorted, so the OLED panel bias cannot be established. The display likely will not function and the short may cause excessive current draw.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomaly detected: the OLED VCOMH node is merged into GND and C11 is connected ground-to-ground, contradicting the specification's intended VCOMH-to-GND reservoir capacitor connection."
}

